# === Acceptance-harness scratch (tools/e2e-m1.ps1) ===
# Only used when the harness is pointed inside the repository, as CI does so its logs can be
# uploaded as an artifact; the local default puts this beside the repository instead.
.e2e-work/

# === Vendored binaries fetched at build time, not committed ===
third_party/nzbget/bin/
third_party/ffmpeg/bin/
# Pebble, fetched by tools/e2e-sidedoor.ps1 (the binary and its public test certificates).
third_party/pebble/bin/

# === Housekeeping scratch (docs/RUNNING.md, docs/UI-LOOP.md): caches, e2e harness work dirs, ===
# === secrets, worktrees, ui-loop/tmp/locks scratch — all git-ignored, none of it committed. ===
.local/

# === Playwright MCP scratch: the page snapshots and screenshots an agent writes while driving ===
# === the web app (docs/UI-LOOP.md). One file per navigation, regenerated every run, and nothing ===
# === in the tree ever reads one back — committing them only makes the tree dirty on every loop. ===
.playwright-mcp/

# === Loose screenshots dropped at the repository root: an agent comparing a UI change before ===
# === and after, or an image saved out of a chat. Root only — the app's real artwork lives under ===
# === apps/stingstream/assets/, and nothing at the top level is ever a committed asset. ===
/*.png

